VeridianOS: FindPerlModules says its per-module checks are named on purpose

For each Perl module it checks (URI::Escape), FindPerlModules.cmake calls
find_package_handle_standard_args() as PerlModules_<module>, to print a
line for it and to set the PerlModules_<module>_FOUND result that the
final HANDLE_COMPONENTS call reads. CMake reports the name differing from
the calling package's ("does not match the name of the calling package
(PerlModules)"). Those calls now pass NAME_MISMATCHED, CMake's way of
declaring that the name differs intentionally; the results are the same.

--- a/cmake/FindPerlModules.cmake
+++ b/cmake/FindPerlModules.cmake
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
             set(PerlModules_all_modules_found FALSE)
         endif()
         find_package_handle_standard_args(PerlModules_${_comp}
+            NAME_MISMATCHED
             FOUND_VAR
                 PerlModules_${_comp}_FOUND
             REQUIRED_VARS
